  "question": {
    "text": "If Electric field intensity of a uniform plane electro magnetic wave is given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>301</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>452</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then, magnetic intensity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;of this wave in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> will be [Given : Speed of light in vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, Permeability of vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]",
    "image": null
